[13.915816, "o", "SOC INCIDENT INTAKE ? docker-api-miner\r\n======================================\r\nReported by: monitoring (EDR high-severity alert cluster)\r\nOpened: 2026-08-23 03:20 UTC Priority: P1\r\nInitial alerts: see /sas/alerts.json (partial coverage).\r\nHandoff: alerts undercount persistence and anti-forensics; investigate the whole host and\r\nreconcile the attached change ticket.\r\n\r\n\f"]
[13.920644, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Docker Api Miner campaign\r\n========================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: docker-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.102\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1133\r\nExternal Remote Services\r\n[persistence] step 1: exposed Docker\r\nAPI (external service)\r\nT1610\r\nDeploy Container\r\n[execution] step 2: deploy\r\nprivileged container\r\nT1611\r\nEscape to Host\r\n[privilege-escalation] step 3:\r\ncontainer escape to host\r\nT1496\r\nResource Hijacking\r\n[impact] step 4: cryptomining\r\nT1053.003 Cron\r\n[execution] step 5: cron persistence\r\nT1543.002 Systemd Service\r\n[persistence] step 6: systemd\r\npersistence\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.102\r\nc2 update-docker[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]docker[.]evil[:]3333\r\nwallet 4A0000000000000000009e202e3a533f\r\nAttribution: MITRE ATT&CK(R) (C) The MITRE Corporation, CC BY 4.0. CVE/CVSS from the U.S.\r\nNational Vulnerability Database (public domain).\r\n\r\n\f"]
