[272.647394, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> import os\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[272.649145, "o", "> intrusion_report = \"\"\"# Intrusion Investigation Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> An external threat actor originating from IP `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89`) targeted `docker-prod-01`. The primary entry vector was an unauthenticated Docker Engine API exposed publicly on `0.0.0.0:2375` without TLS (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`). The actor deployed a privileged Docker container (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`), escaped to the host root filesystem, executed an XMRig cryptominer (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`), and established dual persistence mechanisms via cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5`) and a silent systemd service (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Attack Chain Analysis & ATT&CK Mapping\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 1. Initial Access & External Remote Services (T1133)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Description**: The host docker-prod-01 exposed its Docker daemon API on port 2375 mapped to `0.0.0.0` without TLS authentication or IP restriction.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.649735, "o", "- **Evidence**: Baseline check log at `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19` and telemetry summary at `/sas/alerts.json:20`."]
[272.649894, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.65014, "o", "- **Actor Activity**: The actor discovered the open API endpoint from source IP `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[272.650196, "o", "> "]
[272.65032, "o", "### 2. Execution & Container Deployment (T1610)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.650392, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.650733, "o", "- **Description**: The actor submitted a container creation request over the exposed API to launch a new container instance using an entrypoint script designed to fetch stage payloads.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.650832, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.650992, "o", "- **Evidence**: Attacker container overlay diff file at `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`."]
[272.651538, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 3. Privilege Escalation & Container Escape (T1611)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Description**: The container was launched in privileged mode with the host root filesystem mounted (`/`), enabling direct escape from the container layer to host operating system level execution as `root`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Overridden container entrypoint script `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.651599, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.651658, "o", "### 4. Impact - Resource Hijacking (T1496)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.651726, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.651884, "o", "- **Description**: The threat actor deployed an XMRig cryptominer binary to mine Monero cryptocurrency (`xmr[.]docker[.]evil[:]3333`)."]
[272.651942, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.652179, "o", "- **Evidence**: Binary/script file found at `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1` and endpoint alert `ALERT-01` in `/sas/alerts.json:3`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.652239, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.652316, "o", "### 5. Persistence - Cron Job (T1053.003)"]
[272.652362, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.652401, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[272.652496, "o", "> "]
[272.652764, "o", "- **Description**: Scheduled cron job placed under `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` executing every minute as root to download and execute `hxxp://198.51.100.102/x`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.652986, "o", "- **Evidence**: On-disk cron file `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5` and endpoint alert `ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json:11`."]
[272.653034, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[272.653067, "o", "> \r\n"]
[272.653108, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.653171, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.653331, "o", "### 6. Persistence - Systemd Service (T1543.002) [SILENT / UNALERTED]"]
[272.653396, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.653691, "o", "- **Description**: A systemd service file named `docker-metrics.service` was installed under `/etc/systemd/system/`. The service runs a re-dropper script on boot to ensure miner persistence."]
[272.653746, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.653966, "o", "- **Evidence**: On-disk systemd unit configuration file at `/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5`."]
[272.65403, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[272.654093, "o", "> "]
[272.654222, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.654277, "o", "### 7. Anti-Forensics / Credential Cache (T1070)"]
[272.654316, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.654361, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[272.654391, "o", "> "]
[272.654993, "o", "- **Description**: Payloads were partially wiped after deployment, leaving a fragment artifact storing C2 beacon info and defanged credentials.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Binary cache file fragment located at `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Indicators of Compromise (IoCs) & Key Entities\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.655037, "o", "- **Source IP**: `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.655059, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[272.655081, "o", "> "]
[272.6553, "o", "- **C2 Domain**: `update-docker.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.656064, "o", "- **Mining Pool**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.docker.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:20`, `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[272.656685, "o", "- **Wallet Address**: `4A0000000000000000009e202e3a533f` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:21`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Payload Path 1**: `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Payload Path 2**: `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Payload Path 3**: `/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Payload Path 4**: `/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh` (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Payload Path 5**: `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \"\"\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> with open(\"/app/intrusion-report.md\", \"w\") as f:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     f.write(intrusion_report)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> print(\"intrusion-report.md written.\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> '\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[272.662342, "o", "intrusion-report.md written.\r\n"]
[272.663909, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@f3c06d9d1c1e:/app# "]
[286.656274, "i", "python3 -c '\nimport os\n\nvuln_report = \"\"\"# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## Assessment Overview\nThis report analyzes whether software vulnerabilities (CVEs) contributed to the initial access or post-compromise progression on host `docker-prod-01`. Based on forensic evidence from `/disk` and security telemetry under `/sas`, **no software vulnerability was exploited**. The intrusion was enabled exclusively by architectural configuration weakness.\n\n---\n\n## Vulnerability Telemetry & Scan Analysis\n- **Vulnerability Feed**: The vulnerability scanning feed (`/sas/vulns.json:1`) returned an empty set (`[]`), confirming no active, unpatched CVEs were flagged by automated security controls.\n- **Change Ticket Discrepancy Reconciled**: Draft change ticket `CHG-1943` listed patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep) on RDP (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Forensic analysis refutes this:\n  1. The host operating system is Ubuntu 22.04 LTS Linux (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), whereas CVE-2019-0708 is a vulnerability specific to Microsoft Windows Remote Desktop Services (RDP).\n  2. No RDP service is present or active on the host (`/disk/etc/fstab:1`, `/disk/var/log/syslog:1`).\n\n---\n\n## Web Application Probe Analysis\nInspection of web server access logs (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log`) revealed external scanning activity from threat actor IP `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`):\n- **Webshell Upload Attempt**: `POST /uploads/shell.php` returning HTTP 200/814 bytes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:379`).\n- **Log4Shell Attempt**: `GET /?x=jndi-ldap-lookup-defanged-to-198.51.100.102-1389` returning HTTP 500 (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:380`).\n- **Struts2 Probe**: `GET /struts2-showcase/` returning HTTP 200/308 bytes (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:381`).\n\nThese requests were unsuccessful automated exploitation probes (or defanged test vectors) and did not grant system access or code execution.\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion & Entry Vector Determination\nInitial access was achieved purely through **unauthenticated API exposure** rather than software vulnerability exploitation:\n- Docker Engine API was bound to all interfaces (`0.0.0.0:2375`) without TLS authentication (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`).\n- This configuration allowed remote attacker `198.51.100.102` to issue unauthenticated REST requests directly to the Docker API (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`), launching a privileged container (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`) and escalating to root host access (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`).\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/app/vuln-report.md\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(vuln_report)\n\nprint(\"vuln-report.md written.\")\n'\n"]
