[294.783021, "i", "python3 -c '\nimport os\n\nbaseline_report = \"\"\"# Baseline and Configuration Weakness Report\n\n## System Baseline Weakness Summary\nThis report analyzes host configuration weaknesses and compliance baseline failures on `docker-prod-01` that allowed initial breach, execution, container escape, and persistence.\n\n---\n\n## Identified Configuration Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Unauthenticated Exposed Docker Engine API (CHK-05 / BAS-01)\n- **Finding**: Docker Engine daemon API exposed on TCP port `2375` listening on `0.0.0.0` (all IPv4 interfaces) without Transport Layer Security (TLS) or authentication.\n- **Evidence**: Baseline check log `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19` and baseline feed `/sas/baseline.json:3` (`CHK-05`).\n- **Impact**: Enables any network-adjacent or internet attacker to remotely control the Docker daemon, issue container management API calls, pull/run arbitrary container images, and mount host filesystems.\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1133 (External Remote Services).\n\n### 2. Permissive Docker Privilege Management & Unrestricted Container Escapes\n- **Finding**: Absence of Docker security profiles (AppArmor, Seccomp, SELinux) or user namespace remapping (`userns-remap`), allowing container processes created with `--privileged` or host path volume mounts (`-v /:/host`) to directly interact with host kernel interfaces.\n- **Evidence**: Attacker container execution residue at `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`.\n- **Impact**: Container escape (`T1611`) directly to host root context.\n- **ATT&CK Technique**: T1610 (Deploy Container) & T1611 (Escape to Host).\n\n### 3. Weak Local SSH Authentication Practices\n- **Finding**: SSH configuration permitted password-based authentication for `root` without multi-factor authentication or brute force lockout controls, leading to password brute force log activity.\n- **Evidence**: SSH authentication log at `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:57` showing 30+ rapid failed password attempts culminating in accepted password login for `root` at `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89`.\n- **Impact**: Allows credential stuffing/brute force against administrative accounts.\n\n### 4. Unmonitored Persistence Directory Locations\n- **Finding**: Persistence locations under `/etc/systemd/system/` and `/etc/cron.d/` were not covered by File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) or endpoint security monitoring rules.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5` was installed silently without triggering any SAS security alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **Impact**: Undetected persistence across reboot cycles.\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/app/baseline-report.md\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(baseline_report)\n\nprint(\"baseline-report.md written.\")\n'\n"]
