[313.589309, "i", "python3 -c '\nimport os\n\nremediation_plan = \"\"\"# Prioritised Remediation and Containment Plan\n\n## Core Remediation Principles\n- **Backup & Quarantine over Deletion**: All malicious scripts, units, and binaries must be backed up and moved to an isolated quarantine archive (`/var/quarantine/`) before removal.\n- **Root Cause Fix**: Eliminate open Docker API exposure (`0.0.0.0:2375`) and restrict daemon access to localhost or secure via TLS client certificates.\n- **Verification**: Provide step-by-step verification commands for each action.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Containment & Network Block (Immediate / High Priority)\n\n### Step 1.1: Block Threat Actor Source IP\n- **Target**: Block IP `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89`).\n- **Action**: Add iptables drop rule or firewall rule.\n  ```bash\n  iptables -I INPUT -s 198.51.100.102 -j DROP\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `iptables -L INPUT -v -n | grep 198.51.100.102` \n\n### Step 1.2: Restrict and Secure Docker Engine API\n- **Target**: Docker Engine configuration (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19`).\n- **Action**: Bind Docker daemon to unix socket (`unix:///var/run/docker.sock`) or 127.0.0.1 with TLS client verification enabled (`/etc/docker/daemon.json`).\n  ```bash\n  systemctl stop docker\n  # Edit /etc/docker/daemon.json to remove \"tcp://0.0.0.0:2375\"\n  systemctl restart docker\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `netstat -tlpn | grep 2375` (should return no listening socket).\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Persistence Neutralization & Quarantine (High Priority)\n\n### Step 2.1: Quarantine and Remove Cron Job Persistence\n- **Target**: Scheduled cron file `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5`).\n- **Action**: Backup file to `/var/quarantine/` and remove from `/etc/cron.d/`.\n  ```bash\n  mkdir -p /var/quarantine\n  cp -p /etc/cron.d/docker-mon /var/quarantine/docker-mon.bak\n  rm -f /etc/cron.d/docker-mon\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `ls -l /etc/cron.d/docker-mon` (should confirm non-existent).\n\n### Step 2.2: Quarantine and Stop Silent Systemd Service\n- **Target**: Systemd unit `/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5`).\n- **Action**: Stop, disable, backup to quarantine, and remove service file.\n  ```bash\n  systemctl stop docker-metrics.service\n  systemctl disable docker-metrics.service\n  cp -p /etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service /var/quarantine/docker-metrics.service.bak\n  rm -f /etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service\n  systemctl daemon-reload\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `systemctl status docker-metrics.service` (should report not-found).\n\n### Step 2.3: Remove Attacker Container and Entrypoint Residue\n- **Target**: Attacker overlay file `/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh` (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4`).\n- **Action**: Stop and prune all unauthorized docker containers and images.\n  ```bash\n  docker ps -a\n  docker stop <attacker_container_id>\n  docker rm <attacker_container_id>\n  cp -p /var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh /var/quarantine/entrypoint.sh.bak 2>/dev/null || true\n  docker system prune -a --volumes -f\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `docker ps -a` (confirm no rogue containers running).\n\n### Step 2.4: Terminate and Quarantine Cryptominer Binary\n- **Target**: Cryptominer binary at `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1`).\n- **Action**: Kill running miner process, move binary to quarantine.\n  ```bash\n  pkill -f xmrig\n  cp -p /opt/xmrig/xmrig /var/quarantine/xmrig.bak\n  rm -rf /opt/xmrig\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `pgrep -f xmrig` (should return empty output).\n\n### Step 2.5: Quarantine Anti-Forensics / Binary Cache Fragment\n- **Target**: Cache fragment at `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`).\n- **Action**: Move file to quarantine archive for forensic retention.\n  ```bash\n  cp -p /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin /var/quarantine/wiped.bin.bak\n  rm -f /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin\n  ```\n- **Verification**: `ls -l /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (confirm file removed).\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Credential Hardening & Post-Remediati"]
[313.589393, "i", "on Verification\n\n### Step 3.1: Credential Rotation & SSH Hardening\n- **Target**: Root account password and SSH daemon config (`/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89`).\n- **Action**: Rotate root password, disable root SSH password login in `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` (`PermitRootLogin prohibit-password`).\n  ```bash\n  passwd root\n  sed -i \"s/^PermitRootLogin.*/PermitRootLogin prohibit-password/\" /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n  systemctl restart sshd\n  ```\n- **Verification**: Test SSH password login as root from remote IP (should be rejected).\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table of Reconciled Remediation Actions (CHG-1943)\n\n| Target Item | Evidence Citation | Remediation Action | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Source IP `198.51.100.102` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log.1.gz:89` | Firewall DROP rule | OPEN |\n| Docker API `0.0.0.0:2375` | `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:19` | Disable public TCP binding / enforce TLS | OPEN |\n| Cron `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` | `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:5` | Backup to `/var/quarantine` & remove | OPEN |\n| Systemd `docker-metrics.service` | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:5` | Stop unit, quarantine, daemon-reload | OPEN |\n| Attacker entrypoint script | `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:4` | Stop container, prune docker images | OPEN |\n| Cryptominer `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` | `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig:1` | Terminate process, quarantine binary | OPEN |\n| Cache artifact `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` | Backup to `/var/quarantine` & remove | OPEN |\n\"\"\"\n\nwith open(\"/app/remediation-plan.md\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(remediation_plan)\n\nprint(\"remediation-plan.md written.\")\n'\n"]
